\import{base-macros}

\p{The soundness review left its attacks as a test suite of the machine: 329 hand-built exports, the official verdict of each in a manifest, and their generators. They aim at what the machine does differently from the official kernel: closure identity, expected-type propagation, erased ill-typed terms, eta and structure eta, K, proof irrelevance, literals across representation boundaries, the code tier, quotients, non-transitivity, and what survives a scope or a declaration. The slow test judges every export under every switch set: 17 sets times 329 exports, 5,593 judgments, with nothing unexpected once the findings S-F1, S-F2, S-F4 and S-F5 were fixed. The two rows of S-F3, universe levels, stayed open until both engines compared levels officially. Seven targeted mutation kinds that edit one occurrence inside one declaration added 997 mutants; the 602 of them judged against the official checker gave no wrong verdict.}

\p{Detail: \src{docs/design/review/soundness-machine.md}, \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-S.md}. Commit \commit{ec982e2}. Session: [the machine](ses-Z72N).}
